sentences.l:
For if now beside the ships we were picked, all the best,
for an ambush, where most the excellence of men is made plain,
where the miserable man and the valiant are shown forth:

“Among the middle ships to defend there are others also,
the two Ajaxes, and Teucer, who is best of the Achaeans
in archery, and good also in the standing battle;

And they, when they saw Idomeneus, like flame in might,
himself and his attendant, with wrought gear,
calling out, through the throng upon him all went;
